#document(default_font = "Helvetica", default_size = pt(11), page = { size = "letter" }, margin = { top = pt(72), right = pt(72), bottom = pt(72), left = pt(72) })

LISTS IN TABLES: lists, nested lists and numbered lists inside table cells.

#table(width = pt(468))[
  #row[
    #cell(width = pt(234))[
      - First bullet in a cell.
      - Second bullet in a cell that runs on over more than one line of the narrow column.
        - A nested bullet.
        - Another nested bullet.
      - Third bullet.
    ]
    #cell(width = pt(234))[
      1. First numbered item.
      2. Second numbered item that wraps onto a second line of the cell.
      3. Third numbered item.
    ]
  ]
  #row[
    #cell[A paragraph before a list.

      - Bullet after a paragraph.
      - Another bullet.

      A paragraph after the list.]
    #cell[#ordered_list(start = 4, format = "lower_roman")[
      #item[Fourth in roman.]
      #item[Fifth in roman.]
    ]]
  ]
]

Text after the table.

- A body list before a table.
- Its second item.

| Head | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Alpha | One |
| Beta | Two |

1. A numbered list after a table.
2. Its second item.
